# Docker resolves .dockerignore from the root of the build context, and this service's
# context is ./backend, so this file is what applies; the one at the repo root does not.
# backend/Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into an
# image layer. That includes the gitignored .env holding the Cloudinary, Supabase and Redis
# credentials, and the my_app.log* files, which carry request and user data. Both are
# supplied at run time instead: .env by the bind mount in docker-compose.yml, credentials
# by the environment.
.env
.scheduler.env
*/.env
requirements-dev.txt
.git
my_app.log*
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Not part of the API or scheduler runtime. Exclude test and one-off tooling from
# images; the development Compose bind mount still exposes these files locally.
tests/
app/test.py
seed_db.py
scripts/migrate_account_tables.py
scripts/recreate_chat_schema.py
app/profile_pictures/
